.TH "DEDB" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.20" "dedb Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb \- dedb: DOSEMU2 configuration tooling.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
dedb: DOSEMU2 configuration tooling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V,\fP \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
\fBls\fP
  List downloaded games.
  See \fBdedb-ls(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBls\fP command.
.PP
\fBrun\fP
  Run a game in DOSBox or DOSEMU2.
  See \fBdedb-run(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBrun\fP command.
.PP
\fBdownload\fP
  Download and extract one or more games.
  See \fBdedb-download(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBdownload\fP command.
.PP
\fBrm\fP
  Delete one or more downloaded games' directory trees.
  See \fBdedb-rm(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBrm\fP command.
.PP
\fBrefreshmetadata\fP
  Re-fetch backend metadata for games and rewriting each metadata.json.
  See \fBdedb-refreshmetadata(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBrefreshmetadata\fP command.
.PP
\fBcompletion\fP
  Print a shell completion script for dedb.
  See \fBdedb-completion(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBcompletion\fP command.
.PP
\fBdosboxconf\fP
  Show aspects of a DOSBox config, from dosbox.conf(s) or a game's launch...
  See \fBdedb-dosboxconf(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBdosboxconf\fP command.
.PP
\fBimport\fP
  Create DOSEMU2 config(s) from downloaded games or dosbox.conf files.
  See \fBdedb-import(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBimport\fP command.
.PP
\fBdosemuconf\fP
  Show the converted DOSEMU2 output, from dosbox.conf(s) or a game.
  See \fBdedb-dosemuconf(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBdosemuconf\fP command.
.PP
\fBdownloadgog\fP
  Download and extract DOSBox-based owned games from GOG.
  See \fBdedb-downloadgog(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBdownloadgog\fP command.
.PP
\fBlsgog\fP
  List owned GOG games and whether they look DOSBox-based, without downloading...
  See \fBdedb-lsgog(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBlsgog\fP command.
.PP
\fBlsarchive\fP
  List an archive.org user's favorites as `archive:<id>` targets.
  See \fBdedb-lsarchive(1)\fP for full documentation on the \fBlsarchive\fP command.
